course: dictionary
lesson: 14495
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number, and the words around the word show you which one to use. Peanuts can be a food, or it can mean a very small amount of money.
explain: «We ate peanuts on the walk.» The clues are ate and walk, so peanuts must be the small seeds you can eat. «He gets paid peanuts for all that hard work.» Paid and hard work are the clues, so peanuts here means a very small amount of money.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. If it sounds silly, look for another meaning in the dictionary.
fact: Peanuts are small oval seeds that grow in pods under the ground.
fact: Peanuts are eaten roasted or salted, and they are also made into peanut butter.
fact: A peanut is not a true nut: it is a legume, related to peas and beans.
fact: Informally, «peanuts» can mean a very small amount of money, as in «work for peanuts».
fact: Some people have a peanut allergy, which can be very dangerous. Never share food with a friend who has one, and always check labels.
exercise: «The squirrel hid peanuts under the oak tree.» What are the peanuts here? | A bag of coins | Pods that grow above the ground | Peanut butter sandwiches | *Small seeds you can eat
exercise: «He gets paid peanuts for working all weekend.» What does peanuts mean here? | *A very small amount of money | Shells that grow on bushes | A big prize for working hard | A bag of salted snacks
exercise: Why should you never share your snack with a friend who has a peanut allergy? | *Because peanuts can make them very ill | Because the friend does not like crunchy food | Because peanut snacks go stale quickly | Because peanuts are too expensive to share
test: Where do peanuts grow? | *Under the ground, in pods | In the sea | High up in the trees | On top of tall bushes
test: «They sold their old bikes for peanuts.» What does peanuts mean? | *A very small amount of money | Baskets of seeds | Peanut butter | Lots of money
exam: Which statement about peanuts is true? | Peanuts are sweet fruits that grow on bushes | Peanuts are true nuts that grow on trees | Peanuts always mean a small amount of money | *Peanuts are seeds from pods that grow under the ground
